---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the Lavya website handles your information. The appointment form opens WhatsApp and does not store data on this site."
  noindex
>
  <header class="editorial-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="editorial-hero__title display" data-split="lines">What happens to your details.</h1>
      <p class="editorial-hero__lede" data-reveal="up">
        The short version: this website does not run accounts, store form entries or track you
        across other sites.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="editorial-body">
    <div class="wrap editorial-grid">
      <div class="editorial-grid__main prose">
        <h2>The appointment form</h2>
        <p>
          The form on the contact page does not send data to a server. It builds a message in
          your browser and opens WhatsApp, where you can review and send it yourself. The
          message then sits in your WhatsApp conversation with Lavya, subject to WhatsApp's own
          terms.
        </p>

        <h2>What we keep</h2>
        <p>
          If you call, email or message the salon, we keep the details you choose to share so we
          can confirm and remember your appointment. We do not sell or rent those details.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not set advertising cookies and does not include third party analytics.
          Fonts and images are served from this domain.
        </p>

        <h2>Photography</h2>
        <p>
          Service photographs on this site are supplied by Lavya. They are not presented as
          named clients or team members.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Write to <a class="inline-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
          <a class="inline-link" href={`tel:${site.phoneHref}`}> {site.phone}</a>. We will answer
          directly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
